{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":66266685,"ns":0,"title":"Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Barmak","revisions":[{"revid":1374633449,"parentid":1288882821,"minor":false,"timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:14:16Z","size":3728,"sha1":"588b0fef0941ff485ad0fae87c5f8b79bf6d60f4","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{short description|Chamberlain of Harun al-Rashid from Barmakid family}}\n{{Infobox officeholder\n | name            = Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Barmak\n | image           = \n | alt             = \n | office          = [[Hajib|Chamberlain]] of the [[Abbasid caliph]]\n | term_start      = 788\n | term_end        = 795\n | monarch         = [[Harun al-Rashid]]\n | predecessor     = \n | successor       = [[Al-Fadl ibn al-Rabi]]\n | office2         = \n | term_start2     = \n | term_end2       = \n | monarch2        = \n | predecessor2    = \n | successor2      = \n | office3         = \n | term_start3     = \n | term_end3       = \n | monarch3        = \n | predecessor3    = \n | successor3      = \n | pronunciation   = \n | birth_date      = \n | birth_place     = \n | death_date      = \n | death_place     =\n | death_cause     = illness (natural)\n | children        = \n | father          = [[Khalid ibn Barmak]]\n | mother          =  \n | spouse          = \n}}\n'''Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Barmak''' was one of the [[Barmakids]], a family of [[Iranian peoples|Iranian]] functionaries who rose to great power under the [[Abbasid]] caliph [[Harun al-Rashid]] ({{reign|786|809}}).\n\n==Life==\nHe was the brother of [[Yahya ibn Khalid]],{{sfn|Barthold|Sourdel|1960|p=1036}} whose appointment as [[vizier (Abbasid Caliphate)|vizier]] by Caliph [[Harun al-Rashid]] in 786 began the family's twenty-year domination of the Abbasid Caliphate's public affairs.{{sfn|Barthold|Sourdel|1960|p=1034}} Muhammad served as the Caliph's chamberlain ({{Transliteration|ar|[[hajib]]}}) from 788 to 795.{{sfn|Barthold|Sourdel|1960|p=1036}} He was replaced by [[al-Fadl ibn al-Rabi]],{{sfn|Bosworth|1989|pp=152–153}} who in the anecdotes of the time appears both as the Barmakids' foil and main antagonist at court.{{sfn|Kennedy|2006|pp=33, 79}}\n\nMuhammad also served Harun al-Rashid as governor in the [[Yemen]] and the [[Jazira (caliphal province)|Jazira]].{{sfn|Crone|1980|p=176}}\n\nHe was the only Barmakid to be spared during the family's abrupt fall in 803,{{sfn|Barthold|Sourdel|1960|p=1036}}{{sfn|van Bladel|2012}}{{sfn|Bosworth|1989|pp=219, 222, 224}} likely because he had reported on the attempted flight of the [[Alid]] [[Yahya ibn Abdallah]], who had been released by Yahya's son [[Ja'far ibn Yahya|Ja'far]], contrary to the Caliph's orders to have him killed.{{sfn|Madelung|2002|p=243}}\n\n==Family tree==\n{{Barmakids family tree}}\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist|30em}}\n\n==Sources==\n* {{EI2 | last = Barthold | first = W. | authorlink = Wilhelm Barthold | last2 = Sourdel | first2 = D. | authorlink2 = Dominique Sourdel | title = al-Barāmika | doi =10.1163/1573-3912_islam_COM_0099 | volume = 1 | pages = 1033–1036}}\n* {{The History of al-Tabari|volume=30}}\n* {{Slaves on Horses}}\n* {{cite book | last = Kennedy | first = Hugh | authorlink = Hugh N. Kennedy | title = When Baghdad Ruled the Muslim World: The Rise and Fall of Islam's Greatest Dynasty | location = Cambridge, Massachusetts | publisher = Da Capo Press | year = 2006 | isbn = 978-0-306814808 | url = {{Google books|67fZB5YGkOQC|plainurl=y}} }}\n* {{EI2|volume=11|last=Madelung|first=W.|authorlink=Wilferd Madelung|title=Yaḥyā b. ʿAbd Allāh|pages=242–243|doi=10.1163/1573-3912_islam_SIM_7947}}\n* {{EI3 | last =  van Bladel | first = Kevin | title= Barmakids | doi =10.1163/1573-3912_ei3_COM_24302 | year =2012}}\n\n[[Category:Barmakids]]\n[[Category:8th-century births]]\n[[Category:8th-century people from the Abbasid Caliphate]]\n[[Category:9th-century deaths]]\n[[Category:9th-century people from the Abbasid Caliphate]]\n[[Category:Chamberlains]]\n[[Category:Governors of the Abbasid Caliphate]]\n[[Category:Upper Mesopotamia under the Abbasid Caliphate]]\n[[Category:Abbasid governors of Yemen]]"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-10-30T06:23:02Z","lastrevid":1374633449,"length":3728}]}}